The city attorney shall be the legal advisor and representative of the city and shall:
(1) Advise the mayor, the city council, the chief administrative officer or any city agency head upon all legal questions arising in the conduct of city business;
(2) Prepare or revise ordinances when so requested by the mayor or city council or any committee thereof, review the Code of Ordinances of the city and assist in maintaining an up-to-date code, properly indexed;
(3) Give his official opinion upon any legal matter or question submitted by the mayor or city council;
(4) Attend any city council meeting upon request of the council for the purpose of giving any legal advice required by its members;
(5) Prepare for execution all contracts and instruments to which the city is a party when so requested, and approve as to form all bonds and city contracts;
(6) Defend any and all suits and actions at law or equity brought against the city, unless otherwise directed by resolution of the city council;
(7) Prepare and file any civil suit or action at law or equity to secure or protect the city's best interests, when so ordered by a resolution of the city council;
(8) Make a report to the mayor and the city council on the outcome of any litigation in which the city has a direct interest;
(9) Keep complete and accurate records of the following, which records shall remain the property of the city:
a. All suits in which the city had or has an interest, giving the names of the parties, the nature of the action, the disposition of the case or its status, if pending, and the briefs of counsel; and
b. All written opinions prepared by the city attorney and all certificates or abstracts of titles furnished by the city attorney to the city, or any department or official thereof; and
(10) Render any other legal services as may be required.

