The mayor and city council may grant a waiver from the conflict of interest provision (section 2-113) or the contemporaneous employment provision (section 2-116) upon making a written determination that:
(1) The contemporaneous employment or financial interest of the city elected official, appointed board member, or employee has been publicly disclosed;
(2) The city elected official, appointed board member, or employee will be able to perform its procurement functions without actual or apparent bias or favoritism;
(3) The procurement meets the conditions of the competitive bid process; and
(4) The award will be in the best interest of the city.
(Ord. No. 2015-10, 6-22-2015; Ord. No. 2019-04, 4-8-2019)

